t video that I made and it's  been just wild  it currently has 2.6 million  views which how like how how does that  happen  honestly a lot of it is things to y'all  y'all have watched it or you washed it  shared it and that really helped it to  get basically picked up at a YouTube  algorithm and get millions of views I  remember when I posted it I shared it  with like my Facebook friends and almost  like hey you can watch it that would be  really cool I made a thing honestly one  of the coolest things this last year has  been seeing all the different versions  of a day in the life of a software  engineer seeing people do it in  different cities at different companies  in different roles and every time I see  a new one I get really excited and I  legit like watch all of them other than  that I've learned just a lot in the last  year of being on YouTube I am someone  who does not have any sort of film or  production background so I've learned a  lot about writing and editing it's it's  it's a whole thing to be a youtuber and  I've learned a lot of that I still have  a lot to learn but I am in a much better  place than I was a year ago where I made  my first video on my iPhone 7 using  iMovie and one of my favorite parts of  having been on YouTube for the last year  is that I met so many cool people having  connected with people that I wouldn't  have connected with before or in other  ways and talking about our interests and  love for YouTube basically and also what  we want to do by making videos and just  kind of what our passions are but yeah  honestly that has been such a gift and  that is one of my favorite parts  actually my favorite part about being on  YouTube the other thing I learned after  being on YouTube for the last year is  that I've learned a lot about myself  I joke with people that being on YouTube  has kind of been almost like a form of  therapy for me which is very true  because you see when I was thinking  about like who I am what kind of brand  do I want to have what message do I want  to put out into the world it forced me  to look inside myself and be like okay  well like who are you what are your  values what's important to you what do  you know how to do what do you not know  how to do and I've continually done that  every step in the last year sometimes  feelings so hard like I didn't post the  video November and other times just  succeeding very well and just feeling  very happy about the results it's been  an interesting year because of that  and I definitely would have been a  completely different person honestly if  I hadn't done YouTube and at the end of  the day a lot of the credit goes to you  all you all for watching my videos for  commenting sharing subscribing I  honestly would not be here if it wasn't  for y'all like there's a lot of things  that have happened in the last year that  were thanks to everyone watching and  every single person who has commented  every single person who has messaged me  and said that they feel a little bit  more inspired to do computer science to  just taste their life passions literally  it just kind of kills me inside like in  the best way and I really really want to  thank you at the end of the day I'm just  a girl behind a camera spewing her  thoughts dumping her brain on the  internet and a lot of the strength that  you all have comes from within so thank  you all for sharing that with me and  thank you all for having me be a part of  your journey I would love to know what  you all have thought this last year has  been let me know like when you started  watching my videos and what you like  about them I love hearing people's  stories and I think it's so incredible  that we're all connected through this  way so yeah let me know in the comments  down below send me an Instagram message  send me a Twitter message I genuinely  want to hear from y'all which honestly  has been kind of one of the hardest  parts actually I really appreciate  everyone who has written in so far but  I've had some difficulty just connecting  with people and lots of people at once  I don't think YouTube is super conducive  to that and either in Instagram and  Twitter are okay but this actually leads  into my very first announcement so I  finally have a patreon page which I say  finally because if y'all know me I work  at patreon and I should probably have a  patreon page by now so the reason I want  to have a patreon page is twofold number  one I want to dog food some of the stuff  that me and my team are working on and  really understand what patreon is like  to creators the second one is I really  do want to connect more with more of you  all and I think that patreon is a great  way to build that via a membership  service so I am launching a membership  service essentially so for anywhere from  $1 to more a month then you'll get  access to a bunch of benefits that I  will make exclusive to patreon this also  means that we'll just be able to talk a  lot more I will post  just some thoughts and stuff and more  comments I think it's going to be fun  because it almost be like my safe  sandbox for me to test out ideas and  talk with y'all and interact with you  all in a in just a smaller amount so  there's going to be a lot of cool  benefits one of which is exclusive  content like Bluebird reels and extra  content which I know y'all love and I'll  also be using the lens lenses the  feature that me and my team worked on  for about a year year and a half and I'm  excited to finally use it to interact  with y'all but it's basically like  Instagram stories or snapchat quick  15-second videos that are exclusive just  to my patrons and so I'll be using on  that a ton will also have a benefit  where we will have a private Google  hangout session monthly for folks in a  specific tier which I know that I was  going to do monthly live rooms here on  this channel but honestly they got a  little bit intense and frantic for me  and not so fun anymore  so I'm excite